{title: 631 - When on Life a Darkness Falls}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{tag: Christian Life}
{tag: }

Verse 1:
[F]When on life a darkness [C]falls,
[F]When the mist flows chilling,
[F]Paths and sign posts lost in [C7/Bb]doubt,
[C7]Loveless, [F]unfulfilling,
[F/C]Reach us, Jesus, [Bb]from Your cross,
[Bb]Though [F]we feel forsaken;
[F]Keep us [Gm/Bb]through [C7/Bb]the aching [F]night
[F]Till new dawns awaken.

Verse 2:
[F]When the dreams and vows of [C]youth
[F]Painfully accuse [C]us,
[F]Stab our conscience, steal our [C7/Bb]worth,
[C7]Christ will [F]not refuse [C]us:
[F/C]Peace the world [Bb]cannot provide,
[Bb]Daily [F/C]resurrection,
[F]Strong companion [C7]at our [F]side
[F]For each new direction.

Verse 3:
[F]Come and meet Him, Friend and [C]lord,
[F]Thro' the gospel story:
[F]Open door to life and [C7/Bb]peace,
[C7]Window [F]into glory.
[F/C]All who seek [Bb]Him, soon are found,
[Bb]Made [F]His close relation:
[F]Christ our [Gm/Bb]pathway, [C7]Christ our [F]home,
[F]Christ our sure foundation.
